<title>SINGAPORE: Jurong Cement moves into HK property.</title>
<headline>Jurong Cement moves into HK property.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Building materials company Jurong Cement Ltd said on Friday it would buy 40 percent of Max Billion Finance Ltd (MBFL), a Hong Kong property investment company, for a nominal sum.</p>
<p>Jurong Cement said in a statement MBFL had recently agreed provisionally to buy a Hong Kong property with an area of 20,090 square feet for HK$151.72 million.</p>
<p>Jurong Cement's portion of this investment would be HK$60.69 million. The investment would be financed by bank borrowings and internal resources, it said.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
</text>
